      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve: enrich exported OTEL logs with stable semantics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOperators can keep OTEL diagnostic log bodies private today, but redacted records need stable structure to stay useful. This PR makes ordinary `log.record` diagnostics and trusted `security.event` records queryable by event identity and safe structured attributes without enabling broad log-body capture.\n\nThe stricter requirement is enforced here: OpenClaw-owned calls that emit OTEL `log.record` now need intentional useful semantics, not only a generic exporter fallback. The remaining non-semantic surfaces are explicit pinned exemptions for console/progress/operator-output callbacks and plugin/free-text forwarding boundaries.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDiagnostic log export now reserves OpenClaw-owned semantic fields before generic attributes: `eventName`, `otel.event.name`, `openclaw.signal.type`, and `openclaw.log.*` event/category/outcome/reason/site attributes. Spoofed generic attributes cannot replace those reserved meanings, and attribute-count pressure cannot drop the semantic fields.\n\nOrdinary logs remain redacted by default. Explicit call-site semantics win when present, subsystem/module/plugin/category metadata fills safe diagnostic semantics, and trusted `security.event` records stay separate from message-body semantics while adding `openclaw.security.<action>` event identity to the existing `openclaw.security.*` schema.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can query exported OpenClaw OTEL logs without parsing message text or enabling content capture. Diagnostic records now carry stable fields such as `eventName`, `otel.event.name`, `openclaw.signal.type=log.record`, `openclaw.log.event`, `openclaw.log.category`, `openclaw.log.outcome`, `openclaw.log.reason`, `openclaw.log.site_id`, `openclaw.log.level`, and category/source metadata when available.\n\nSecurity events now use the same top-level event identity shape with `openclaw.signal.type=security.event`, while preserving the trusted security schema. Plugin/free-text logs remain compatible and private: raw message content is not used to infer event names or reason codes, and redacted diagnostic bodies still export as `[message redacted]` unless content capture is intentionally enabled.\n\nAccepted exemption boundary:\n\n- `operator_output_callback: 121` pinned call sites. These are console/progress/operator-output callbacks and are not being converted in this PR.\n- `compat_runtime_adapter: 4` pinned call sites for compatibility runtime adapter logging.\n- Extension plugin/free-text fallback remains pinned by exact counts and fingerprints: `knownCount=382 knownFingerprint=8ed0750b44745cd1`, `injectedCount=428 injectedFingerprint=695ee489eac02cbb`.\n- Plugin logger adapter is not exempt; plugin/runtime logger metadata is wired through the structured logger API and covered by tests.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBehavioral proof:\n\n- Redacted `log.record` exports include `eventName`, `otel.event.name`, `openclaw.signal.type=log.record`, `openclaw.log.event`, `openclaw.log.category`, `openclaw.log.outcome`, `openclaw.log.reason`, and `openclaw.log.site_id` while keeping the body redacted.\n- Capture-enabled `log.record` exports keep the same event identity and semantic attributes while replacing only the body with the log message. This mode is tested only to prove conditional body behavior; it is not required or recommended for normal operation.\n- Trusted `security.event` exports include `eventName=openclaw.security.<action>`, `otel.event.name`, `openclaw.signal.type=security.event`, `body=openclaw.security.event`, and the existing `openclaw.security.*` fields.\n- Exporter tests prove generic attributes cannot spoof reserved semantic keys or the trusted `openclaw.security.*` event namespace.\n- `src/logging/diagnostic-log-site-inventory.test.ts` audits OpenClaw-owned log sites across `src`, `extensions`, `packages`, and `ui`, and fails if owned OTEL-emitting logs lose explicit semantics or if pinned exemptions drift.\n\nRepresentative exported shapes:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"severityText\": \"INFO\",\n  \"eventName\": \"openclaw.plugins.start.info\",\n  \"body\": \"[message redacted]\",\n  \"signalType\": \"log.record\",\n  \"event\": \"plugins.start.info\",\n  \"category\": \"plugins\",\n  \"outcome\": \"success\",\n  \"reason\": \"none\",\n  \"siteId\": \"837e22f502a9a100\",\n  \"bodyRedacted\": true,\n  \"codeFunction\": \"start\"\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"severityText\": \"INFO\",\n  \"eventName\": \"openclaw.heartbeat.runner.started\",\n  \"body\": \"[message redacted]\",\n  \"signalType\": \"log.record\",\n  \"event\": \"heartbeat.runner.started\",\n  \"category\": \"gateway.heartbeat\",\n  \"outcome\": \"success\",\n  \"reason\": \"configured\",\n  \"siteId\": \"959451e6fedb25e7\",\n  \"bodyRedacted\": true,\n  \"codeFunction\": \"updateConfig\"\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"severityText\": \"WARN\",\n  \"eventName\": \"openclaw.security.gateway.auth.failed\",\n  \"body\": \"openclaw.security.event\",\n  \"signalType\": \"security.event\",\n  \"action\": \"gateway.auth.failed\",\n  \"category\": \"auth\",\n  \"outcome\": \"denied\",\n  \"severity\": \"medium\",\n  \"reason\": \"token_mismatch\",\n  \"actorKind\": \"operator\",\n  \"targetKind\": \"gateway\",\n  \"policyDecision\": \"deny\",\n  \"controlFamily\": \"auth\"\n}\n```\n\nAutomated checks:\n\n- Targeted regression suite passed: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/commands-plugin.test.ts src/infra/heartbeat-runner.commitments.test.ts src/infra/heartbeat-runner.timeout-warning.test.ts src/logging/diagnostic-log-site-inventory.test.ts src/logging/diagnostic-log-events.test.ts src/logger.test.ts src/logging/subsystem.test.ts src/logging/level-filter.test.ts src/plugins/logger.test.ts src/plugins/runtime/runtime-logging.test.ts src/plugins/runtime/runtime-logging.integration.test.ts extensions/diagnostics-otel/src/service.test.ts test/scripts/changed-lanes.test.ts` passed 7 shards / 279 tests.\n- `corepack pnpm plugin-sdk:api:check` passed after regenerating the plugin SDK API baseline for the updated plugin logger semantics.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` passed after the final amend.\n- Code-review workflow completed clean: Phase 1 native review reached 3 clean passes after accepted findings were fixed; Phase 2 cold review reached a clean independent pass after accepted findings were fixed.\n- Broad changed gate passed on Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kwtnyxnhg4cbewy5m1z543wf`: `check:changed` completed successfully against the amended PR head.\n\nNo screenshots: this is backend/exporter/logging behavior and docs; there is no human-visible UI state to capture.\n",
